  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Organisations pay for smooth operations and happy customers. They judge you by reliability, accuracy and calm under pressure.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is keeping a schedule where nothing falls through.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and business administration in healthcare and sports: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools draft schedules and messages. Routine coordination shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    People handling, judgment and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to draft and check; later, own operations.
  </p>

